From 6c0624cb4d85c364c9de388fc3da2357ebba8c0e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: axfor <aixiaoxiang2009@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 22:21:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] promscrape: support zstd-compressed scrape responses

Adds -promscrape.zstdCompression, off by default. With it on, the request
carries Accept-Encoding: zstd, gzip; a target answering with zstd is
decompressed as zstd, and gzip or no compression behaves as upstream does.

ReadData returns the response's Content-Encoding ("gzip" / "zstd" / "")
instead of an isGzipped bool, and readFromBuffer picks the decompressor
from it.
